  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Solar Action Program (ASAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASAP aims to mobilize concessional finance to mainstream Solar PV investments among urban and grid-connected MSMEs and households, contributing to the reduction of Ghana&#x2019;s GHG emissions, and creating a favourable environment for sustainable energy financing over the long term. 

&#x2022; The programme has strong climate basis, which envisions improving Ghana&#x2019;s heavily fossil-fuel reliant energy mix especially amid the reduced hydropower capacity of the country due to climate change impacts.
&#x2022; Concessionality passed on to end beneficiaries, with the potential to generate cost savings while the AE takes on end-beneficiary credit risk
&#x2022; With a comprehensive approach to developing local markets for Solar PV projects and capacity building, the programme has replication potential, potentially showcasing successful solar PV systems industry growth and expansion.</narrative>
  </description>
